  "presentation_summary": [
    "A 72-year-old man presented with three days of worsening cough with green sputum, shortness of breath, and generalized weakness.",
    "Presentation vitals were HR 107/min, BP 151/84 mmHg, SpO2 96% on room air, RR 20/min, and temperature 37.2 C.",
    "He denied chest pain, fever, nausea, vomiting, bloody sputum, dizziness, weight loss, chills, night sweats, recent travel, sick contacts, steroid use, IV drug use, COVID infection, prior TB, and HIV.",
    "Exam was notable for decreased breath sounds bilaterally, right basal rhonchi, cachexia/malnutrition, and poor oral hygiene.",
    "Labs showed WBC 19.2 x10^9/L, bicarbonate 17 mmol/L, and lactate 1.7 mmol/L.",
    "Chest X-ray showed right lower-lobe consolidation; CT showed a 4.5 x 4.1 x 6.5 cm right lower-lobe cavitary lesion with air-fluid level, smooth enhancing wall, adjacent tree-in-bud opacities, nodules up to 1.3 cm, loculated empyema, and thickened pleura.",
    "The initial differential included cavitary pneumonia, aspiration-related abscess, tuberculosis, and malignancy."
  ],
